<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak central bank says sees no crown devaluation.</title>
<headline>Slovak central bank says sees no crown devaluation.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) sees no reason to devalue the crown in the foreseeable future, a senior NBS official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We will not consider crown devaluation in the foreseeable future, as we have sufficient hard currency reserves currently covering about 3.6 months of imports,&quot; NBS Vice-governor Marian Jusko told journalists at a finance conference in Bratislava.</p>
</text>
